From db9f9d9d738732d10c97194d50214bdf00a4414c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 19:54:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/28] Drone: gentler sidechain ducking, reverb send without
 double song volume; review fixes; grain LFO init

- Drone ducking is linear instead of squared (user feedback: 30 lost too much): 30 dips to -8 dB at the bottom of a
  full hit instead of -16 dB, 50 still ducks fully; the knob popup shows the dip in dB.
- The drone's reverb send takes the song volume out once, since the reverb output gets it again in renderSongFX().
- Pulse edges: the 1 ms minimum can't exceed half a cycle at extreme beats (clamp with lo > hi).
- Attack/Release show as percent on the 7-segment display too.
- Song automation no longer overwrites the drone view's knob indicators.
- 1.2.1 fix: the mod FX LFO wave type was uninitialised for GRAIN.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eb214cM1zi1k5Gpcn9RLKh
